\[
|\mathcal D_{n,m}|\le {n+m\choose m}.
\]
For fixed \(d\in\mathcal D_{n,m}\), the variables
\[
X_t(d)=A_t1\{A_t<d_t\}
\]
are independent and lie in \([0,1]\), with mean \(g(d_t)\). Hoeffding gives
\[
\Pr\left\{
\sum_t X_t(d)<\sum_t g(d_t)-u
\right\}\le \exp(-2u^2/n).
\]
