## Finite LP, Interval, And Approximation Background

- Fulkerson and Gross (Pacific Journal of Mathematics 1965), "Incidence matrices and interval graphs," is verified. It is relevant background for consecutive-ones/interval-incidence structure in the finite-alphabet dual, but it does not imply the desired uncrossing/localization theorem because the market dual has nested maxima.
